{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1094", "sample_idx": 45, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "```json\n{\n  \"famous_moms_extraordinaire\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Patti Smith\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"Punk rock’s poetic first lady, also the mom of Jesse Paris Smith (who’s a rapper, so… legacy!). Genre-blending icon, self-described ‘rock poet,’ and still writing at 75—basically the OG ‘I’ll never grow up’ mom.\",\n      \"random_fact\": \"She recited William Blake at CBGB before punk even had a glow-up. Also, her ‘Horses’ album cover? A baby in a can. *Iconic.*\",\n      \"mom_energy\": \"‘I didn’t have time for motherhood until after I destroyed the patriarchy.’ —Patti, probably\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Jada Pinkett Smith\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"Actress, producer, fashionista, and queen of the ‘I raised Will Smith like a boss’ vibes. Also, the mom who turned ‘I’ll spare you’ into an art form (see: the *Madagascar* franchise).\",\n      \"random_fact\": \"She once wore the same *Red Bottoms* for *10 years* straight because ‘comfort is key.’ Mom goals.\",\n      \"mom_energy\": \"‘You will *not* be taking my son’s crown.’ —Jada, every time.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Taylor Swift\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"The folk-pop princess who went from ‘Tim McGraw’ to ‘Anti-Hero’ *and* ‘Mom Who Rewrote a Song About Her Baby.’ Also, the only mom to make ‘I’m a mom now’ a cultural reset button.\",\n      \"random_fact\": \"Her first child’s nursery theme was *literally* a ‘folklore’ cottagecore dream. Crib included a tiny guitar and a ‘Renaissance fair’ vibe. *Yes, ma’am.*\",\n      \"mom_energy\": \"‘I wrote a *10-minute* song about my kid’s nap schedule. *Bless you, baby.*’ —Taylor, probably between takes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Sigourney Weaver\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"Alien-slaying, Oscar-winning badass who also birthed two kids while keeping the ‘I’m older than your problems’ energy.